# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# File Purpose
#   This is a template file for defining sensitive environment variables,
#   API keys, and authentication tokens.
#
# Problems Solved
#   - Prevents hardcoding secrets in version-controlled scripts.
#   - Centralizes authentication tokens for various CLI tools.
#   - Avoids "Rate Limit Exceeded" errors for unauthenticated API calls.
#
# Features / Responsibilities
#   - AI/LLM Provider configuration.
#   - Development tool authentication (GitHub, Homebrew).
#   - Instructions for securing file permissions.
#
# Usage Notes
#   1. Copy:  mv env.example $ZDOTDIR/.env
#   2. Edit:  $EDITOR $ZDOTDIR/.env (Fill in your real keys)
#   3. Secure: chmod 600 $ZDOTDIR/.env (Read/Write for owner ONLY)
#   4. Ignore: Ensure '.env' is added to your .gitignore file.
#   5. Add Keys: Uncomment/add your own vars with keys.
#
# Project: Zsh-conf
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

#

# Global Configuration
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
## This file is intended to be 'sourced' by your shell profile (.zshrc).
## Variables defined here become available to terminal commands.

# ── ai & llm services ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Configuration for Generative AI tools and CLI wrappers.
# Many CLI tools (like 'gh', 'fabric', or custom scripts) look for these
# specific variable names automatically.

# OpenAI (ChatGPT, Codex, Whisper)
# Required by: generic LLM wrappers, auto-coders.
# OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"

# Anthropic (Claude)
# Required by: Claude CLI, research tools.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"

# Google (Gemini, PaLM)
# Required by: Google Cloud SDK, Gemini CLI tools.
# GEMINI_API_KEY="XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"


# ── development tools ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Authentication tokens to increase API quotas and enable write access.

# GitHub Token
# Scope: Should generally include 'repo', 'workflow', and 'user'.
# Used by: gh cli, git-credential-manager.
# GITHUB_TOKEN="ghp_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"

# Homebrew GitHub Token
# Purpose: Homebrew downloads formulas from GitHub. Unauthenticated requests
# are heavily rate-limited. Setting this prevents 403 errors during updates.
# HOMEBREW_GITHUB_API_TOKEN="ghp_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"


# ── custom secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# User-defined variables for local scripts or private projects.

# Example: A secret key for a local Docker container or internal tool.
# APP_INTERNAL_SECRET="some-secret-value"
